// Title: Arbitrary File Download Via MSPUB.EXE
// Sigma ID: 3b3c7f55-f771-4dd6-8a6e-08d057a17caf
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: 2023-02-08
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects usage of "MSPUB" (Microsoft Publisher) to download arbitrary files
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/pull/238/files
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_mspub_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\MSPUB.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "MSPUB.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "ftp://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")
